  "body": "I entered two rooms (picantly the Matrix-HQ-Forum and the Element-Web/Desktop-Forum) recently. One day later, I was not able to read and write new messages there (my first thought was, I was banned - so I've tried the to contact admins). One admin told me, that it seems to be the consequence of a dirty room-update...\r\n\r\nA few days later, I tried to leave both rooms, and to re-enter. But I was still in the \"twilight-zone\" between in and out. \r\n\r\nThe most meaningful error-message was:\r\n\"\r\nMatrixError: [404] Not a known room (https://synapse.matrix.digitale-gesellschaft.ch/_matrix/client/r0/rooms/!YTvKGNlinIzlkMTVRl%3Amatrix.org/leave)\r\n\".\r\n\r\nFinally, I was re-invited in both rooms and after about an hour (in the case of the Matrix-HQ-Foum) of struggling while connecting the forums and server-fetching-errors, it worked then. \r\n\r\nIt looked a bit like, my home-server (digitale-gesellschaft.ch) had to be restarted than (because of my requests of the Matrix-HQ-Forum???), before the things began to run...\r\n\r\nAccording to \"https://wiki.asra.gr/en:public_servers\", a \"Synapse 1.66.0\" is running at digitale-gesellschaft.ch.",
